<title>USA: Owens-Illinois offers 14.75 million shares.</title>
<headline>Owens-Illinois offers 14.75 million shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOLEDO, Ohio 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Owens-Illinois Inc said on Tuesday it will make a public offering of 14.75 million common shares priced at $28.50 apiece, under the company's $2.5 billion shelf registration of April 18.</p>
<p>The company said the proceeds will be used to refinance outstanding public debt.</p>
<p>Managing underwriters are Salomon Brothers, Goldman Sachs, Lehman Brothers, Merrill Lynch, Morgan Stanley and PaineWebber.</p>
<p>Owens-Illinois shares closed Monday at 28-1/2. The company makes glass bottles and containers and other products.</p>
